OpenTUI third-party notices
==============================

The compiled workgate OpenTUI client includes or links code from the
following locked packages. Versions are taken from ui-opentui/bun.lock.

- @opentui/core 0.4.3 — MIT
- @opentui platform-native core packages 0.4.3 — MIT
- @opentui/react 0.4.3 — MIT
- react 19.2.0 — MIT
- react-reconciler 0.33.0 — MIT
- scheduler 0.27.0 — MIT
- ansi-regex 6.2.2 — MIT
- bun-ffi-structs 0.2.4 — MIT
- csstype 3.2.3 — MIT
- emoji-regex 10.6.0 — MIT
- get-east-asian-width 1.6.0 — MIT
- marked 17.0.1 — MIT
- react-devtools-core 7.0.1 — MIT
- shell-quote 1.10.0 — MIT
- string-width 7.2.0 — MIT
- strip-ansi 7.1.2 — MIT
- web-tree-sitter 0.25.10 — MIT
- ws 7.5.11 and 8.21.0 — MIT
- diff 9.0.0 — BSD-3-Clause

TypeScript 5.9.3 is an Apache-2.0-licensed build-time tool and is not shipped as
an independent runtime component. `bun build --compile` embeds the pinned Bun
1.3.14 runtime in the executable. Bun itself is MIT-licensed, while its official
license record identifies statically linked JavaScriptCore/WebKit under LGPL-2,
tinycc under LGPL-2.1, and additional linked libraries under their listed terms.
The verbatim `bun-v1.3.14` `LICENSE.md` is distributed beside this notice as
`BUN-1.3.14-LICENSE.md` and inside Python packages as
`workgate/helpers/bun-1.3.14.LICENSE.md`. It includes the corresponding
WebKit source and relink instructions. Redistributors remain responsible for the
LGPL object/relink and source-availability obligations described there.

